1
00:00:02,180 --> 00:00:05,100
=The Truth (Season 4)=
(Behind-the-Scenes Cast Interview)

2
00:00:05,160 --> 00:00:07,480
(Li Fei as Leader Li)
How did it feel dancing to "I'm Li Fei"?

3
00:00:08,160 --> 00:00:08,990
I couldn't even imagine it.

4
00:00:09,320 --> 00:00:10,590
I'd never even thought about it.

5
00:00:10,600 --> 00:00:14,390
Dancing with all these guys...

6
00:00:14,400 --> 00:00:15,750
They're people I normally

7
00:00:16,200 --> 00:00:17,870
only see on TV.

8
00:00:17,880 --> 00:00:19,910
Here, I'll show you the proper way.

9
00:00:20,080 --> 00:00:21,110
I'm Li Fei,

10
00:00:21,120 --> 00:00:21,990
no backbone.

11
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:22,750
Unmoved by gain or loss,

12
00:00:22,760 --> 00:00:23,830
joy or sorrow.

13
00:00:23,840 --> 00:00:26,350
I thought everyone did great.

14
00:00:26,360 --> 00:00:27,310
I feel like

15
00:00:27,320 --> 00:00:28,590
they'd all heard of it before.

16
00:00:29,440 --> 00:00:30,550
I was seriously so excited.

17
00:00:30,560 --> 00:00:30,910
Perfect.

18
00:00:32,710 --> 00:00:33,380
Perfect.

19
00:00:33,720 --> 00:00:34,910
Especially Ding.

20
00:00:35,280 --> 00:00:37,550
This was basically
an online-friends meetup for us.

21
00:00:37,560 --> 00:00:38,950
Alright, handsome guy.

22
00:00:38,960 --> 00:00:40,150
I'm Li Fei,

23
00:00:40,160 --> 00:00:40,870
no backbone.

24
00:00:40,880 --> 00:00:41,630
Unmoved by gain or loss,

25
00:00:41,640 --> 00:00:42,750
joy or sorrow.

26
00:00:43,060 --> 00:00:44,200
(Nailed it)

27
00:00:44,200 --> 00:00:46,470
Why does his look better
than the original?

28
00:00:46,470 --> 00:00:47,320
(Clearly practiced at home)

29
00:00:47,320 --> 00:00:49,870
You've secretly practiced this,

30
00:00:49,880 --> 00:00:50,630
haven't you?

31
00:00:50,640 --> 00:00:51,390
Loved it to "death".

32
00:00:52,120 --> 00:00:53,350
No problem.

33
00:00:53,600 --> 00:00:54,150
Not bad.

34
00:00:54,320 --> 00:00:56,750
We'd only interacted online before.

35
00:00:57,360 --> 00:00:58,110
But, well...

36
00:00:58,400 --> 00:00:59,990
Seeing him in person,

37
00:01:00,140 --> 00:01:00,840
he's handsome.

38
00:01:00,840 --> 00:01:02,430
And his moves were spot-on.

39
00:01:02,440 --> 00:01:03,630
And when I said,

40
00:01:03,640 --> 00:01:05,510
"You should teach me sometime, "

41
00:01:05,519 --> 00:01:06,310
I really meant it.

42
00:01:07,440 --> 00:01:09,030
As for everyone else,

43
00:01:09,040 --> 00:01:10,910
He just looked cool.

44
00:01:10,920 --> 00:01:11,750
He danced so well.

45
00:01:12,400 --> 00:01:13,350
I'm Li Fei,

46
00:01:14,280 --> 00:01:14,910
no backbone.

47
00:01:14,920 --> 00:01:15,510
Unmoved by gain or loss,

48
00:01:15,510 --> 00:01:16,200
joy or sorrow.

49
00:01:16,200 --> 00:01:17,590
Next one.

50
00:01:17,590 --> 00:01:18,800
(This one's even worse)

51
00:01:18,800 --> 00:01:19,270
I can tell.

52
00:01:19,280 --> 00:01:20,270
He really does look spineless.

53
00:01:21,520 --> 00:01:22,070
At the time,

54
00:01:22,560 --> 00:01:24,150
I actually wanted to see it again.

55
00:01:24,160 --> 00:01:25,790
But I moved on.

56
00:01:25,800 --> 00:01:27,350
Then when we came back,

57
00:01:27,720 --> 00:01:28,350
I forgot

58
00:01:28,360 --> 00:01:29,870
to make him do it again.

59
00:01:29,880 --> 00:01:31,910
I really hadn't seen enough.

60
00:01:31,920 --> 00:01:33,470
(The real reason)
When we danced I'm Li Fei,

61
00:01:33,480 --> 00:01:34,870
I was totally hyped.

62
00:01:34,880 --> 00:01:35,470
So excited.

63
00:01:35,480 --> 00:01:37,430
(Adrenaline took over)
My mind basically went blank.

64
00:01:37,760 --> 00:01:39,830
I didn't even know what I was saying.

65
00:01:39,840 --> 00:01:41,550
So whatever I said about everyone

66
00:01:41,560 --> 00:01:43,350
might not even be true.

67
00:01:43,360 --> 00:01:45,550
(Please forgive me)
I was just way too hyped then.

68
00:01:46,280 --> 00:01:47,590
(Inner thoughts:)
With everyone doing it,

69
00:01:47,600 --> 00:01:48,870
the dance looked so cool.

70
00:01:48,880 --> 00:01:50,830
(Everyone killed it)
They made me feel like this dance

71
00:01:51,880 --> 00:01:53,750
was some amazing

72
00:01:53,760 --> 00:01:54,790
choreography.

73
00:01:56,760 --> 00:01:58,190
They took something

74
00:01:58,200 --> 00:02:00,110
pretty ordinary

75
00:02:00,120 --> 00:02:01,150
(And him?)
and leveled it up.

76
00:02:01,720 --> 00:02:02,430
I was so happy.

77
00:02:03,200 --> 00:02:04,490
It was your first time on The Truth,

78
00:02:04,490 --> 00:02:05,960
and you were the culprit.
How did that feel?

79
00:02:05,960 --> 00:02:07,470
Being the culprit was like this.

80
00:02:09,479 --> 00:02:12,150
Five minutes before I said that,

81
00:02:12,160 --> 00:02:13,710
(Found out right before the trial)
I was the culprit.

82
00:02:13,720 --> 00:02:15,710
I was completely shocked.

83
00:02:16,240 --> 00:02:17,230
I honestly thought

84
00:02:17,240 --> 00:02:18,030
they'd told everyone

85
00:02:18,040 --> 00:02:18,950
the same thing

86
00:02:18,960 --> 00:02:20,230
just to film our reactions.

87
00:02:20,240 --> 00:02:21,750
Because I had no idea.

88
00:02:21,760 --> 00:02:23,390
I seriously had no idea.

89
00:02:23,400 --> 00:02:24,790
Then I started piecing together

90
00:02:24,800 --> 00:02:25,750
why it was me

91
00:02:25,760 --> 00:02:26,270
and what I'd done.

92
00:02:26,280 --> 00:02:27,750
Then it finally clicked.

93
00:02:27,760 --> 00:02:29,220
It really was me.

94
00:02:29,220 --> 00:02:29,760
(I'm really the culprit)

95
00:02:29,760 --> 00:02:32,190
It was this huge lightbulb moment.

96
00:02:32,200 --> 00:02:32,750
So I think

97
00:02:32,760 --> 00:02:34,230
that's something The Truth 4

98
00:02:34,240 --> 00:02:36,470
does really well.

99
00:02:36,480 --> 00:02:37,070
Basically,

100
00:02:37,080 --> 00:02:38,710
they actually manage

101
00:02:38,720 --> 00:02:40,750
to keep the actors in the dark

102
00:02:40,760 --> 00:02:41,830
and let you keep acting.

103
00:02:41,840 --> 00:02:43,070
Then they tell you later.

104
00:02:43,080 --> 00:02:44,110
That way,

105
00:02:44,560 --> 00:02:45,830
your whole mindset

106
00:02:45,840 --> 00:02:47,710
is completely different

107
00:02:47,720 --> 00:02:49,110
from when you know the script.

108
00:02:49,120 --> 00:02:50,550
You get way more immersed,

109
00:02:50,560 --> 00:02:52,830
and the audience gets pulled in too.

110
00:02:53,500 --> 00:02:55,340
(What's happening?)

111
00:02:55,360 --> 00:02:56,700
(Even the lights got immersed)
They got into it too.

112
00:02:57,080 --> 00:02:58,680
Which comedian would you
recommend for The Truth?

113
00:02:59,440 --> 00:03:00,590
Zhang Xingchao.

114
00:03:00,600 --> 00:03:01,830
(That's me)
Because he scares easily.

115
00:03:02,400 --> 00:03:04,230
Honestly, scaring Zhang Xingchao

116
00:03:04,240 --> 00:03:06,190
could be its own show.

117
00:03:06,200 --> 00:03:07,670
Just call it "Scare Zhang Xingchao".

118
00:03:07,680 --> 00:03:09,030
The way he looks when he's scared

119
00:03:09,040 --> 00:03:10,030
is hilarious.

120
00:03:11,340 --> 00:03:12,500
(Night vision mode. Meanwhile...)

121
00:03:12,520 --> 00:03:13,310
What's going on?

122
00:03:15,260 --> 00:03:15,860
(That got him)

123
00:03:16,030 --> 00:03:17,110
Away from the comedy stage,

124
00:03:17,110 --> 00:03:18,830
you played a totally new role
on a variety show.

125
00:03:18,830 --> 00:03:20,260
What's different between the two?

126
00:03:22,160 --> 00:03:23,390
I think

127
00:03:23,400 --> 00:03:25,030
the main difference is

128
00:03:25,040 --> 00:03:26,070
with this kind of acting,

129
00:03:26,080 --> 00:03:28,230
after you improvise,

130
00:03:28,240 --> 00:03:29,470
you have to get back into the scene.

131
00:03:29,880 --> 00:03:32,350
So we act,

132
00:03:32,360 --> 00:03:32,790
improvise,

133
00:03:32,800 --> 00:03:33,590
then get back into the scene.

134
00:03:33,600 --> 00:03:34,830
Then improvise and jump back in again.

135
00:03:34,840 --> 00:03:36,550
I think it's really hard.

136
00:03:37,040 --> 00:03:37,870
Because when you're

137
00:03:37,880 --> 00:03:39,110
improvising,

138
00:03:39,120 --> 00:03:42,430
you have to pick up
on everything the players give you.

139
00:03:42,440 --> 00:03:43,230
And you also

140
00:03:43,720 --> 00:03:45,150
have to stay in character.

141
00:03:45,160 --> 00:03:46,670
Ideally, you never break character.

142
00:03:46,680 --> 00:03:48,070
But what's similar

143
00:03:49,120 --> 00:03:50,510
is you still have to build a character.

144
00:03:50,520 --> 00:03:51,950
What kind of person are you?

145
00:03:51,960 --> 00:03:53,350
What role are you playing

146
00:03:53,360 --> 00:03:55,190
when you talk to these people?

147
00:03:55,200 --> 00:03:57,030
While building

148
00:03:57,040 --> 00:03:58,710
Leader Li,

149
00:03:58,720 --> 00:04:00,910
I still had to stay close
to the players,

150
00:04:00,920 --> 00:04:03,350
then slip back into character.

151
00:04:03,360 --> 00:04:05,670
There was also this long monologue.

152
00:04:05,680 --> 00:04:06,830
In Chinese pinyin,

153
00:04:06,840 --> 00:04:07,390
it's

154
00:04:07,390 --> 00:04:08,520
"ai".

155
00:04:08,520 --> 00:04:10,870
It represents the "love" in our hearts.

156
00:04:10,880 --> 00:04:11,590
So

157
00:04:12,200 --> 00:04:13,190
this place

158
00:04:13,200 --> 00:04:15,430
is your safest haven!

159
00:04:15,440 --> 00:04:16,470
It's your vault!

160
00:04:16,480 --> 00:04:18,430
It's the home you

161
00:04:18,880 --> 00:04:19,589
can never leave!

162
00:04:21,680 --> 00:04:23,710
That scene was really fun to perform.

163
00:04:24,560 --> 00:04:26,190
I really treated it

164
00:04:26,200 --> 00:04:27,590
like a little stage play.

165
00:04:29,360 --> 00:04:30,750
When I got the script,

166
00:04:30,760 --> 00:04:31,470
I thought

167
00:04:31,480 --> 00:04:33,550
my character was really well-developed.

168
00:04:33,560 --> 00:04:34,590
He had everything.

169
00:04:34,600 --> 00:04:35,630
The whole character bio

170
00:04:35,640 --> 00:04:36,510
the directors wrote for me

171
00:04:36,520 --> 00:04:37,710
was really good.

172
00:04:37,720 --> 00:04:39,710
(Thumbs up)
It felt really complete.

173
00:04:39,720 --> 00:04:41,670
That gives an actor a lot to work with.

174
00:04:42,360 --> 00:04:42,950
So,

175
00:04:42,960 --> 00:04:46,030
throughout the whole game,

176
00:04:46,040 --> 00:04:46,870
whether

177
00:04:47,260 --> 00:04:48,000
you're...

178
00:04:48,000 --> 00:04:48,470
Whether you're

179
00:04:48,480 --> 00:04:49,350
a player,

180
00:04:49,360 --> 00:04:50,430
an NPC,

181
00:04:50,440 --> 00:04:51,470
or

182
00:04:51,480 --> 00:04:54,390
anyone involved in the show,

183
00:04:54,400 --> 00:04:56,510
I was completely immersed in it.

184
00:04:58,290 --> 00:05:00,660
How would Leader Li promote The Truth?

185
00:05:00,660 --> 00:05:01,360
What would you say?

186
00:05:04,600 --> 00:05:06,510
Want a great show?

187
00:05:06,520 --> 00:05:09,750
Go watch it on WeTV.

188
00:05:09,760 --> 00:05:11,150
The Truth 4.

189
00:05:11,600 --> 00:05:12,630
Don't be fooled

190
00:05:12,640 --> 00:05:13,830
by how run-down

191
00:05:13,840 --> 00:05:14,750
this place looks.

192
00:05:14,760 --> 00:05:15,790
What's inside

193
00:05:15,800 --> 00:05:16,950
is pure gold.

194
00:05:18,180 --> 00:05:20,380
(Fu Jiahua as the new leader)
Who screamed loudest in the dark?

195
00:05:22,160 --> 00:05:23,230
Sun Qian.

196
00:05:23,680 --> 00:05:25,670
The second the lights went out,

197
00:05:26,480 --> 00:05:29,030
I felt like before she even entered,

198
00:05:29,040 --> 00:05:30,950
she'd already warmed up her voice.

199
00:05:30,960 --> 00:05:31,470
Open the door.

200
00:05:32,980 --> 00:05:33,470
Come in.

201
00:05:33,700 --> 00:05:38,380
(Channel One, Channel Two,
Channel Three)

202
00:05:38,900 --> 00:05:40,380
(Frozen in place)

203
00:05:40,400 --> 00:05:41,430
What do I do?

204
00:05:41,600 --> 00:05:43,590
The other players were scared too,

205
00:05:43,920 --> 00:05:45,470
but she was so terrified

206
00:05:45,800 --> 00:05:47,150
that everyone else

207
00:05:47,760 --> 00:05:48,390
started comforting her

208
00:05:48,400 --> 00:05:49,550
and forgot their own fear.

209
00:05:49,900 --> 00:05:51,320
When testing players on their names,

210
00:05:51,320 --> 00:05:52,220
would you go easy on them?

211
00:05:52,240 --> 00:05:54,110
Not really.

212
00:05:54,120 --> 00:05:55,310
We still wanted

213
00:05:55,680 --> 00:05:56,830
to get some

214
00:05:56,840 --> 00:05:58,470
fun, genuine reactions.

215
00:05:58,480 --> 00:05:59,750
But today,

216
00:05:59,760 --> 00:06:02,070
when they checked their own names,

217
00:06:02,080 --> 00:06:02,950
I didn't

218
00:06:02,960 --> 00:06:04,430
try to stop them.

219
00:06:04,440 --> 00:06:05,630
Because what I'd ask

220
00:06:05,640 --> 00:06:07,290
wouldn't be
about their own names anyway.

221
00:06:07,400 --> 00:06:09,190
Once they memorized their names,

222
00:06:09,200 --> 00:06:10,550
we'd just

223
00:06:10,560 --> 00:06:11,350
change the question on the spot.

224
00:06:11,680 --> 00:06:12,910
For example, we'd ask,

225
00:06:12,920 --> 00:06:14,060
(Thinking on the fly)
"What's the person next to you called?"

226
00:06:14,080 --> 00:06:15,870
So all that time they spent memorizing
their own name

227
00:06:15,880 --> 00:06:17,670
suddenly

228
00:06:17,680 --> 00:06:18,590
made it even funnier.

229
00:06:18,800 --> 00:06:19,950
Okay, listen up.

230
00:06:19,950 --> 00:06:21,120
Three, two, one.

231
00:06:21,120 --> 00:06:22,540
(Caught off guard)
What's his name?

232
00:06:25,360 --> 00:06:26,150
His name is...

233
00:06:27,800 --> 00:06:31,070
Proudblood, Ruthless Duke, Mad Dragon.

234
00:06:31,080 --> 00:06:31,630
Right?

235
00:06:33,120 --> 00:06:33,790
He got it right.

236
00:06:35,620 --> 00:06:36,980
(All that memorizing paid off)

237
00:06:38,200 --> 00:06:40,150
Proudblood, Ruthless Duke, Mad Dragon.

238
00:06:40,800 --> 00:06:43,230
He remembered everyone else's
names pretty well.

239
00:06:43,240 --> 00:06:45,110
He really put in the work.

240
00:06:45,120 --> 00:06:45,470
Seriously.

241
00:06:46,150 --> 00:06:48,320
Any funny moments from filming?

242
00:06:48,360 --> 00:06:50,350
Today, the players
had bags over their heads,

243
00:06:50,360 --> 00:06:51,870
and we guided them forward.

244
00:06:51,880 --> 00:06:52,770
Great.

245
00:06:55,620 --> 00:06:56,420
Where are we?

246
00:06:56,440 --> 00:06:57,510
Keep walking.

247
00:06:57,520 --> 00:06:59,430
After we came out of the passage,

248
00:07:00,120 --> 00:07:01,470
Liu Yuning

249
00:07:01,480 --> 00:07:03,350
asked me what was up ahead.

250
00:07:03,360 --> 00:07:05,150
So I quietly messed with him.

251
00:07:05,160 --> 00:07:06,430
I said there's a cliff ahead.

252
00:07:06,720 --> 00:07:08,110
I didn't think he'd believe me.

253
00:07:08,120 --> 00:07:09,710
Then as I walked away,

254
00:07:09,720 --> 00:07:11,230
I heard him tell the players behind him.

255
00:07:11,240 --> 00:07:11,790
I heard him.

256
00:07:11,800 --> 00:07:12,990
He said, "Don't push me!"

257
00:07:13,000 --> 00:07:14,190
"There's a cliff ahead!"

258
00:07:14,870 --> 00:07:15,270
Yeah.

259
00:07:16,090 --> 00:07:17,720
Did any of the players' reactions

260
00:07:17,720 --> 00:07:19,060
really stand out during filming?

261
00:07:19,520 --> 00:07:20,150
Yeah.

262
00:07:21,120 --> 00:07:21,790
Here's what happened.

263
00:07:21,800 --> 00:07:24,990
We had the players go in groups of three

264
00:07:26,360 --> 00:07:27,670
onto this lift.

265
00:07:27,680 --> 00:07:28,870
And I was playing

266
00:07:28,880 --> 00:07:29,830
the villain.

267
00:07:29,840 --> 00:07:31,350
(Classic villain)
A very stereotypical villain.

268
00:07:31,360 --> 00:07:33,630
As they got onto the lift,

269
00:07:33,640 --> 00:07:35,390
I'd say,

270
00:07:35,600 --> 00:07:36,750
"Watch your head."

271
00:07:37,000 --> 00:07:39,430
Then Ding Chengxin
turned around and said,

272
00:07:39,800 --> 00:07:41,150
"Why are you actually kinda nice?"

273
00:07:41,640 --> 00:07:42,710
And I thought,

274
00:07:42,720 --> 00:07:43,590
that's totally out of character.

275
00:07:43,600 --> 00:07:44,350
So I quickly added,

276
00:07:44,760 --> 00:07:45,990
"I still need your brains."

277
00:07:46,000 --> 00:07:46,590
Got it.

278
00:07:47,400 --> 00:07:49,590
I think every player's improv reactions

279
00:07:49,600 --> 00:07:50,470
including Jin Jing's

280
00:07:50,480 --> 00:07:51,310
were

281
00:07:51,320 --> 00:07:52,190
so good.

282
00:07:52,200 --> 00:07:53,190
Their improv skills

283
00:07:53,200 --> 00:07:53,950
were amazing too.

284
00:07:57,620 --> 00:07:58,570
=The Truth (Season 4)=

285
00:07:58,580 --> 00:07:59,660
(SVIP updates Wed & Thu at noon)

286
00:07:59,670 --> 00:08:00,740
(VIP updates next day at noon,
one week early)
